WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.535
-Welcome back to the show,
buddy.

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:04.037
I appreciate you being here.
-Thanks for having me back.

00:00:04.037 --> 00:00:05.472
It's so nice to see you
and hug you.

00:00:05.472 --> 00:00:07.073
-And hug you, yeah. And slow
dance with you. It felt great.

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:08.374
-Yeah, that's really
the reason I came.

00:00:08.374 --> 00:00:09.309
I felt like I should just go.

00:00:09.309 --> 00:00:10.810
-Yeah, every time.

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:14.013
Who better to have on Broadway
Week than Ben Platt?

00:00:14.013 --> 00:00:15.882
Thank you for being here.
-Thank you.

00:00:15.882 --> 00:00:17.183
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:19.853
-Broadway reopened last night.

00:00:19.853 --> 00:00:21.487
-Yes.
-You already saw a show.

00:00:21.487 --> 00:00:22.922
-I went to the reopening
of "Wicked."

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:23.857
-No way!
-Yes.

00:00:23.857 --> 00:00:25.825
-Good for you.
-Yeah, "Wicked"!

00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:27.193
-How was it?

00:00:27.193 --> 00:00:28.794
-It was like a crazy exp--

00:00:28.794 --> 00:00:30.596
I feel like I'm still
sort of vibrating from it

00:00:30.596 --> 00:00:32.198
'cause it was like
a rock concert.

00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:35.101
Like, every other line got
a standing ovation and a scream.

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:37.102
It took like an hour
to get to the first song.

00:00:37.102 --> 00:00:39.205
[ Laughter ]
It was incredible.

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:40.874
Like, when she flies at the end
of the first act,

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:42.508
everybody just kind of was,
"Oh, we're all going to stand.

00:00:42.508 --> 00:00:44.043
Okay," and everybody
just kind of stood

00:00:44.043 --> 00:00:46.545
and watched it from standing,
but it was a dream come true.

00:00:46.545 --> 00:00:48.114
And I got to be with
my boyfriend, Noah,

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:49.782
who came with me,
and we love "Wicked" together,

00:00:49.782 --> 00:00:50.950
so it's great.
-Come on. Congrats.

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:53.352
[ Cheers and applause ]
That's great.

00:00:53.352 --> 00:00:56.055
Last time you were on Broadway,
you won a Tony, my man.

00:00:56.055 --> 00:00:57.523
Not bad.
-Yeah, I did. Thanks.

00:00:57.523 --> 00:01:00.526
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:00.526 --> 00:01:02.796
-Do you remember the feeling
after, like,

00:01:02.796 --> 00:01:04.229
Tina Fey gave you the Tony?

00:01:04.229 --> 00:01:06.532
Do you remember exactly
what happened in your mind?

00:01:06.532 --> 00:01:09.302
-Yeah, it was like, "Okay.
Hello, Tina Fey. Hello, Tony."

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:12.338
And then yelled my speech
as fast as I could.

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:14.840
And they tried to play me off,
but I made it to the end.

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:17.343
And then, I walked off stage,
and Lin-Manuel was just --

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:18.945
Lin-Manuel Miranda
was just standing there,

00:01:18.945 --> 00:01:21.047
waiting to go
and present the next award.

00:01:21.047 --> 00:01:23.449
And so I just kind of
instinctively kind of just went

00:01:23.449 --> 00:01:25.218
into his arms and he sort of
just hugged me.

00:01:25.218 --> 00:01:26.352
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:28.120
And then, there was
a photographer backstage

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:29.789
who immediately was like,
"Let me just snap a pic."

00:01:29.789 --> 00:01:31.591
And I, like, turn and took
the picture with him.

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:33.493
And I -- it's online somewhere,
but it's --

00:01:33.493 --> 00:01:35.227
I look like I just smoked
a ton of crack.

00:01:35.227 --> 00:01:36.662
It's just like --
-Yeah, I know.

00:01:36.662 --> 00:01:39.966
It's not even online. I have it.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:41.400
-Oh, yeah.
-There you are, there. Yeah.

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:43.703
[ Laughter ]
You're really psyched.

00:01:43.703 --> 00:01:45.104
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:45.104 --> 00:01:47.807
You're really -- You're really
into it. Wow.

00:01:47.807 --> 00:01:49.209
You're really excited
about that.

00:01:49.209 --> 00:01:50.743
-It was really intense.
So that's -- Yeah.

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:52.745
That really sums it up.
-We had Beanie Feldstein

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:54.514
on the show last week, who I
know you've known for a --

00:01:54.514 --> 00:01:56.282
[ Audience cheers ]
Yeah, we love her.

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:59.185
And she's great in the new
"Impeachment."

00:01:59.185 --> 00:02:00.719
-Amazing.
Her performance is incredible.

00:02:00.719 --> 00:02:02.955
-Amazing.
You and her were prom dates.

00:02:02.955 --> 00:02:04.624
-We were prom dates. Yes.

00:02:04.624 --> 00:02:06.492
-I did not know who you --
I saw it on your wall,

00:02:06.492 --> 00:02:08.460
I think, last time you did
our show from home.

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:10.396
And I saw it in your house. I
was like, "Wait, what is that?"

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:11.965
-Yeah, we were best friends
in high school,

00:02:11.965 --> 00:02:14.300
and we were prom dates, and my
favorite part about that now

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:18.037
is that when I asked her
to prom, I sent her flowers,

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:19.939
and I wrote a little card
that said --

00:02:19.939 --> 00:02:21.306
Beanie loves "Funny Girl,"

00:02:21.306 --> 00:02:22.909
which for those who don't know,
she's going to star

00:02:22.909 --> 00:02:24.076
in "Funny Girl" on Broadway
this year.

00:02:24.076 --> 00:02:26.479
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:28.181
Which is wild.
-Yeah.

00:02:28.181 --> 00:02:30.082
-And I always knew she loved
"Funny Girl," so it said like,

00:02:30.082 --> 00:02:32.218
"Don't rain on my parade.
Please come to prom with me."

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:33.086
-No way.
[ Audience aws ]

00:02:33.086 --> 00:02:34.387
-And now she's Fanny Brice.

00:02:34.387 --> 00:02:36.555
Here's the picture.
Here's your prom photo.

00:02:36.555 --> 00:02:38.458
-Uh-huh.
-Look at this.

00:02:38.458 --> 00:02:41.060
-There's prom dates right there.
That's what I'm talking about.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:43.630
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yes. We're doing the --

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:45.865
-Did you both always --
-Eva Peron arms.

00:02:45.865 --> 00:02:48.334
-Did you always both have dreams
of being on Broadway?

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:50.703
-Yes, absolutely. We were
big theater nerds together.

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:52.772
We starred in all the musicals
together in high school.

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:54.173
And it was always our dream.

00:02:54.173 --> 00:02:57.110
Actually, for my 16th birthday,
she gave me cuff links.

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:59.078
And she gave me a little note
that I have saved that said,

00:02:59.078 --> 00:03:01.180
"Wear these when you win
your first Tony," and I did.

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:03.849
[ Audience aws ]
And I wore them at Radio City.

00:03:03.849 --> 00:03:05.118
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Dude, that is the best!

00:03:05.118 --> 00:03:07.519
I love that story!

00:03:07.519 --> 00:03:10.389
That's so cool, man.
-Thanks.

00:03:10.389 --> 00:03:13.025
-You released your new album,
"Reverie."

00:03:13.025 --> 00:03:15.061
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah.

00:03:15.061 --> 00:03:17.129
People love it,
and you're going on tour.

00:03:17.129 --> 00:03:18.998
This poster is
all over New York City.

00:03:18.998 --> 00:03:20.966
I don't know if you have seen it
on the side of the Garden.

00:03:20.966 --> 00:03:23.669
It is gigantic.
A giant Ben Platt.

00:03:23.669 --> 00:03:24.937
-Just my armpit.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.937 --> 00:03:26.138
-It's just the armpit.
That's it.

00:03:26.138 --> 00:03:28.474
The rest is covered over.
But this is big, man.

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:30.142
-It's cool. It's really cool.

00:03:30.142 --> 00:03:31.778
-You're playing big arenas.
-Yeah.

00:03:31.778 --> 00:03:33.979
I mean, I've never played
my original music

00:03:33.979 --> 00:03:35.515
in spaces this big.

00:03:35.515 --> 00:03:37.316
The biggest place I think
I've ever played is

00:03:37.316 --> 00:03:39.152
when I was nine years old,
I did the Hollywood Bowl

00:03:39.152 --> 00:03:41.053
because I was in "The Music Man"
there, the musical.

00:03:41.053 --> 00:03:43.056
I played the little kid,
Winthrop, in it.

00:03:43.056 --> 00:03:44.790
And so I'm playing that again
on the tour.

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:46.292
So it's sort of like
a little full circle

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:48.194
back to the Bowl
as myself little moment.

00:03:48.194 --> 00:03:49.661
-I thought you were playing
Winthrop.

00:03:49.661 --> 00:03:51.030
-Yeah, yeah, no, I'm actually
just touring --

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:52.198
[ Laughter ]
-You're doing "Music Man"?

00:03:52.198 --> 00:03:53.900
-Just the Winthrop material
from "Music Man."

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:55.868
[ Laughter ]
-That's the tour?

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:57.069
But this is major, dude.
-Thanks.

00:03:57.069 --> 00:03:58.404
-I love this move, by the way.

00:03:58.404 --> 00:04:00.105
Were you on a trampoline here?

00:04:00.105 --> 00:04:01.540
-Just straight from the ground.

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:03.943
-Straight-from-the-ground jump.
-On my own natural high.

00:04:03.943 --> 00:04:05.277
[ Laughter ]
Yeah.

00:04:05.277 --> 00:04:06.579
Just trying to give
like a Springsteen,

00:04:06.579 --> 00:04:08.180
kind of Peter Gabriel,
a little Phil Collins vibe.

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:09.582
-Yeah, I got that vibe.

00:04:09.582 --> 00:04:11.317
Have you been watching
any shows,

00:04:11.317 --> 00:04:13.552
getting inspiration
for your tour?

00:04:13.552 --> 00:04:16.889
-Well, I -- my dream for the
tour is to combine, like,

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:19.458
all my favorite pop shows I've
seen, like Beyoncé and Ariana.

00:04:19.458 --> 00:04:21.360
Like the shows
that are big spectacles

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:23.696
and got everybody up moving
and a lot of tempo.

00:04:23.696 --> 00:04:25.932
And then also my other favorite
show I ever saw at the Garden

00:04:25.932 --> 00:04:27.467
was Barbra Streisand, of course.

00:04:27.467 --> 00:04:29.235
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yes, Barbra!

00:04:29.235 --> 00:04:31.537
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.537 --> 00:04:34.440
And she makes the whole giant
stadium feel like

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:35.908
you're all in her living room.
-Yeah, she does.

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:38.444
-It's just so intimate and,
like, she's telling so much

00:04:38.444 --> 00:04:41.147
honest stories and making you
laugh and so off-the-cuff.

00:04:41.147 --> 00:04:42.681
So I'd love to find,
like, a beautiful,

00:04:42.681 --> 00:04:44.484
little middle ground, where we
can, like, party and dance

00:04:44.484 --> 00:04:46.619
but also, like, I can tell
my secrets and stuff.

00:04:46.619 --> 00:04:47.853
And it'll be fun.

00:04:47.853 --> 00:04:49.188
-Buddy, congrats on this tour
and the album.

00:04:49.188 --> 00:04:50.356
-Thanks.

00:04:50.356 --> 00:04:51.724
-I want to talk about
"Dear Evan Hansen."

00:04:51.724 --> 00:04:54.126
This is in theaters next Friday.

00:04:54.126 --> 00:04:56.329
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:56.329 --> 00:04:58.230
Next Friday. It's happening.

00:04:58.230 --> 00:04:59.632
-It's happening, finally. Yes.

00:04:59.632 --> 00:05:01.100
-When you did the play,

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:02.968
you don't think that
it's going to be a movie.

00:05:02.968 --> 00:05:04.137
You just hope the play is good.

00:05:04.137 --> 00:05:06.472
-Exactly, yeah. It's so rare
that a musical

00:05:06.472 --> 00:05:08.307
gets the privilege
of becoming a film

00:05:08.307 --> 00:05:10.276
and even rarer
that somebody is allowed

00:05:10.276 --> 00:05:12.044
to transfer the performance
onto film.

00:05:12.044 --> 00:05:14.580
So I never assumed that this
would happen and -- and I --

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:16.716
you know, I dreamt about it when
the show started getting big

00:05:16.716 --> 00:05:18.718
and people started loving it,
but I did not --

00:05:18.718 --> 00:05:20.186
especially once the pandemic
started, I was like,

00:05:20.186 --> 00:05:21.387
"Well, now this is
never going to happen."

00:05:21.387 --> 00:05:24.156
But Universal and
the director and the writers,

00:05:24.156 --> 00:05:26.659
everybody was really focused on
getting this story done

00:05:26.659 --> 00:05:28.461
'cause they thought it was
really important for right now.

00:05:28.461 --> 00:05:31.196
It's all about, you know,
everyone's universal experience

00:05:31.196 --> 00:05:34.033
of isolation and loneliness and
the need for human connection.

00:05:34.033 --> 00:05:36.402
And I feel like, unfortunately
right now, that's, like,

00:05:36.402 --> 00:05:38.404
even more important than it was
when the show came out.

00:05:38.404 --> 00:05:40.339
So I'm just grateful that
it came together

00:05:40.339 --> 00:05:42.375
and they let me do it.
-I got to see you on Broadway.

00:05:42.375 --> 00:05:45.411
I was lucky.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:45.411 --> 00:05:46.778
It's great.

00:05:46.778 --> 00:05:48.581
I got to see you perform.

00:05:48.581 --> 00:05:51.016
I was lucky enough to see you
on Broadway, and man, oh man,

00:05:51.016 --> 00:05:53.353
I was like, "Dude, just stop,"
after the second song.

00:05:53.353 --> 00:05:55.120
I go, "This guy's unbelievable,
man.

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:56.722
Just stop. We're good.
Just stop, man."

00:05:56.722 --> 00:05:58.156
[ Laughter ]

00:05:58.156 --> 00:06:00.159
I heard that when you were
shooting the movie,

00:06:00.159 --> 00:06:02.828
they yelled "cut" after a scene,
and then they had to stop

00:06:02.828 --> 00:06:04.330
because all the crew
were crying.

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:07.466
People had to, like -- The boom
guy had to wipe his tears.

00:06:07.466 --> 00:06:09.235
It was like, "Alright,
everyone, regroup.

00:06:09.235 --> 00:06:10.303
We got to do another take."

00:06:10.303 --> 00:06:12.805
-Yeah, it was
a very emotional setting.

00:06:12.805 --> 00:06:15.107
I mean, this is my director
Stephen Chbosky's story, really,

00:06:15.107 --> 00:06:17.142
but I'll steal it, which is
that, on the second day,

00:06:17.142 --> 00:06:18.911
I was doing one of the songs.
It's called, "Words Fail."

00:06:18.911 --> 00:06:20.079
It's kind of one of the darker,

00:06:20.079 --> 00:06:21.613
kind of more difficult,
emotional songs.

00:06:21.613 --> 00:06:23.582
And the first take
I performed it,

00:06:23.582 --> 00:06:24.616
and it was very early on
in the shoot,

00:06:24.616 --> 00:06:25.851
so a lot of the crew in Atlanta

00:06:25.851 --> 00:06:26.885
didn't know
what they were in for.

00:06:26.885 --> 00:06:28.420
So I sang the song,

00:06:28.420 --> 00:06:30.623
and then there was a lot of
silence after the cut.

00:06:30.623 --> 00:06:32.658
And no one really said anything,
and then an unidentified

00:06:32.658 --> 00:06:34.693
crew member who we love
but we don't know who it was,

00:06:34.693 --> 00:06:36.162
came over the walkie
and just went,

00:06:36.162 --> 00:06:37.363
"Well, this is going to
be a good movie."

00:06:37.363 --> 00:06:39.064
[ Laughter ]

00:06:39.064 --> 00:06:41.100
-That's it. That's what you
need. That's a good omen.

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:42.801
The walkie says so.

00:06:42.801 --> 00:06:44.169
You got to believe it.

00:06:44.169 --> 00:06:45.471
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:45.471 --> 00:06:47.606
Here's Ben Platt
in "Dear Evan Hansen."

00:06:47.606 --> 00:06:49.642
Take a look at this.

00:06:49.642 --> 00:06:52.812
♪ -Even when the dark
comes crashing through ♪

00:06:52.812 --> 00:06:56.582
♪ When you need a friend
to carry you ♪

00:06:56.582 --> 00:07:00.419
♪ And when you're broken
on the ground ♪

00:07:00.419 --> 00:07:02.922
♪ You will be found ♪

00:07:02.922 --> 00:07:05.724
♪ So let the sun come
streaming in ♪

00:07:05.724 --> 00:07:08.861
♪ 'Cause you'll reach up
and you'll rise again ♪

00:07:08.861 --> 00:07:12.365
♪ Lift your head
and look around ♪

00:07:12.365 --> 00:07:18.370
♪ You will be fooooound ♪

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:23.776
♪ You will be foooooound ♪

00:07:23.776 --> 00:07:29.114
♪ You will be foooooooound ♪

00:07:29.114 --> 00:07:34.620
♪ You will be foooooound ♪

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:37.089
♪ You will be found ♪

00:07:37.089 --> 00:07:39.858
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah. Come on, now.

00:07:39.858 --> 00:07:42.461
You got it. Ben Platt!

00:07:42.461 --> 00:07:45.565
"Dear Evan Hansen" is in
theaters September 24th.

